Input: {"question": "Where is the Grist Mill Bridge located?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 0, "end": 231, "text": "Grist Mill Bridge, Dam and Mill Site The Grist Mill Bridge, Dam and Mill Site consists of three structures located along Upton Road between Island Road and the Maple River, one-half mile west of Elsie, Michigan in Duplain Township."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 232, "end": 337, "text": "The three structures are: The structures were listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2015."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 338, "end": 386, "text": "Duplain Township was first settled in the 1830s."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 387, "end": 411, "text": "In about 1845, Robert E."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 412, "end": 500, "text": "Craven (likely with his brothers Joseph and Thomas) constructed a saw-mill at this site."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 501, "end": 543, "text": "The saw mill operated for nearly 20 years."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 544, "end": 566, "text": "In 1865, Kellogg Bros."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d00", "start": 567, "end": 597, "text": "and Johnson purchased the site"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d01", "start": 0, "end": 271, "text": "Grist Mill Covered Bridge The Grist Mill Covered Bridge, also known as the Scott Covered Bridge, the Bryant Covered Bridge, and the Canyon Covered Bridge, is a covered bridge that carries Canyon Road across the Brewster River, off Vermont Route 108 in Cambridge, Vermont."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d01", "start": 272, "end": 416, "text": "Built in the 19th century, it is one of a small number of surviving Burr arch truss bridges in the state, and is one of three left in Cambridge."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d01", "start": 417, "end": 483, "text": "It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1974."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d01", "start": 484, "end": 574, "text": "The Grist Mill Covered Bridge is located south of the village of Jeffersonville, on Canyon"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d02", "start": 0, "end": 51, "text": "and records noting replacement of its deck in 1885."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d02", "start": 52, "end": 240, "text": "Documentary references to bridges at or near this location were also made in 1792 and 1822, but none of the documentation predating 1885 is conclusively connected to the present structure."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d02", "start": 241, "end": 360, "text": "The stonework of the bridge supports bears some resemblance to that of the mill foundation and what remains of its dam."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d02", "start": 361, "end": 463, "text": "The bridge's oldest features are its abutments and single pier, all of which are dry laid rubblestone."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d02", "start": 464, "end": 540, "text": "These elements place the wooden bridge deck about above typical water level."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d02", "start": 541, "end": 605, "text": "The southern abutment includes a wing wall that extends for some"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0459-cd4f437f7154:d03", "start": 0, "end": 125, "text": "��F����\u00059